# Code owners for vault-desktop.
#
# A PR touching any path below requests review from the listed person.
#
# NOTE ON TEAM SLUGS: this file originally listed @functionfly/platform and
# @functionfly/security, copied from the monorepo. The `functionfly` org has
# NO teams (`gh api /orgs/functionfly/teams` returns `[]`), so every one of
# those handles was unresolvable. CODEOWNERS with an unresolvable owner is
# silently ignored by GitHub, which means "required approvals" backed by it
# would never be satisfiable and merges would hang with no explanation.
# The two real repository collaborators are used instead.
#
# When the org does grow teams, prefer team slugs over individuals: review
# requests survive someone leaving the project.
#
# Current collaborators:
#   functionflycom  — repo admin, org owner account
#   CallReef        — collaborator
#
# Default owners for anything not matched below.
*                                       @functionflycom

# ── Security-sensitive surfaces ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Rust core owns the crypto primitives, the keychain, and the HTTP client
# that attaches the bearer token. A change here alters the trust boundary
# between the vault and the orchestrator.
/src-tauri/src/crypto.rs                 @functionflycom
/src-tauri/src/store.rs                  @functionflycom
/src-tauri/src/api.rs                    @functionflycom
/src-tauri/src/updater.rs                @functionflycom
/src-tauri/src/commands/                 @functionflycom

# Capability manifest: this file decides what the webview is allowed to do.
# Widening it is a privilege-escalation change and needs a deliberate review.
/src-tauri/capabilities/                 @functionflycom

# Wire-format compatibility with the dashboard and the Go SDK. Any edit here
# can break cross-client secret decryption.
/src/lib/ipc.ts                          @functionflycom

# ── Release pipeline ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The signing key, the updater manifest layout, and the release scripts are
# the supply chain for every shipped binary.
/scripts/release/                        @functionflycom
/.github/workflows/                      @functionflycom
/.github/codeql/                         @functionflycom

# ── Frontend ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/src/screens/                            @functionflycom
/src/App.tsx                             @functionflycom
/src/styles.css                          @functionflycom

# ── Release metadata ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These four are bumped together by release-please. A PR that touches one of
# them without the others desynchronises the release.
/CHANGELOG.md                            @functionflycom
/package.json                            @functionflycom
/src-tauri/Cargo.toml                    @functionflycom
/src-tauri/tauri.conf.json               @functionflycom